#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The examples in this section illustrate some common ways to use the Executor"
" primitive. Before running these examples, follow the instructions in "
"[Install Qiskit](/guides/install-qiskit) and [Executor "
"quickstart](/guides/directed-execution-model).\n"
msgstr ""
"Les exemples de cette section illustrent quelques façons courantes "
"d'utiliser la primitive Executor. Avant d'exécuter ces exemples, suis les "
"instructions dans [Installer Qiskit](/guides/install-qiskit) et [Démarrage "
"rapide avec Executor](/guides/directed-execution-model).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Before you begin {#before-you-begin}"
msgstr "Avant de commencer {#before-you-begin}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Some of the code examples on this page use `samplex`, which is part of the "
"Samplomatic package.  Therefore, before running those code block, you must "
"install Samplomatic, as shown in the following code block.  For more "
"information, see the [Samplomatic "
"documentation](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic).\n"
msgstr ""
"Certains des exemples de code sur cette page utilisent `samplex`, qui fait "
"partie du package Samplomatic. Par conséquent, avant d'exécuter ces blocs de"
" code, tu dois installer Samplomatic, comme indiqué dans le bloc de code "
"suivant. Pour plus d'informations, consulte la [documentation "
"Samplomatic](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Example: Parameterized circuit {#example-parameterized-circuit}"
msgstr "Exemple : Circuit paramétré {#example-parameterized-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This example illustrates how to add circuit items with parameters, as well as how to add samplex items. It consists of these steps:\n"
"1. Set up the circuit: Generate and transpile the target circuit.\n"
"2. Prepare a samplex: Group gates and measurements into annotated boxes and generate the circuit template and samplex pair.\n"
"3. Execute: Add a circuit item and a samplex item to a `QuantumProgram` and execute both in a single job.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cet exemple illustre comment ajouter des éléments de circuit avec des paramètres, ainsi que comment ajouter des éléments samplex. Il comprend ces étapes :\n"
"1. Configurer le circuit : Générer et transpiler le circuit cible.\n"
"2. Préparer un samplex : Regrouper les gates et les mesures dans des boîtes annotées et générer la paire circuit template et samplex.\n"
"3. Exécuter : Ajouter un élément de circuit et un élément samplex à un `QuantumProgram` et exécuter les deux dans un seul job.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set up the circuit {#set-up-the-circuit}"
msgstr "Configurer le circuit {#set-up-the-circuit}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Prepare a three-qubit GHZ state, rotate the qubits around the Pauli-Z axis, "
"and measures the qubits in the computational basis.\n"
msgstr ""
"Préparer un état GHZ à trois qubits, faire pivoter les qubits autour de "
"l'axe de Pauli-Z, et mesurer les qubits dans la base computationnelle.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Specify the backend and transpile the circuit to only use instructions "
"supported by the QPU (referred to as an instruction set architecture (ISA) "
"circuit).\n"
msgstr ""
"Spécifier le backend et transpiler le circuit pour n'utiliser que les "
"instructions supportées par le QPU (appelé circuit d'architecture d'ensemble"
" d'instructions (ISA)).\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare the samplex {#prepare-the-samplex}"
msgstr "Préparer le samplex {#prepare-the-samplex}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the `generate_boxing_pass_manager` convenience function and its twirling"
" parameters to group two-qubit gates and measurements into boxes and apply "
"twirling annotations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Utiliser la fonction de commodité `generate_boxing_pass_manager` et ses "
"paramètres de twirling pour regrouper les gates à deux qubits et les mesures"
" dans des boîtes et appliquer des annotations de twirling.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the `build` method to generate the template circuit and the samplex.\n"
msgstr ""
"Utiliser la méthode `build` pour générer le circuit template et le "
"samplex.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Execute the circuits {#execute-the-circuits}"
msgstr "Exécuter les circuits {#execute-the-circuits}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Executor runs `QuantumProgram` objects. Each `QuantumProgram` can contain "
"several items. This example adds a circuit item and a samplex item for "
"execution. For full details, see [Executor input and "
"output](/guides/executor-input-output).\n"
msgstr ""
"Executor exécute des objets `QuantumProgram`. Chaque `QuantumProgram` peut "
"contenir plusieurs éléments. Cet exemple ajoute un élément de circuit et un "
"élément samplex pour l'exécution. Pour tous les détails, voir [Entrée et "
"sortie de l'Executor](/guides/executor-input-output).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first step is to initialize an empty program, requesting `1024` shots "
"for each configuration of each item.\n"
msgstr ""
"La première étape est d'initialiser un programme vide, en demandant `1024` "
"shots pour chaque configuration de chaque élément.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Append the circuit item to the `QuantumProgram`. This circuit item consists "
"of two parts - the ISA circuit and 10 sets of its parameter values.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ajouter l'élément de circuit au `QuantumProgram`. Cet élément de circuit est"
" composé de deux parties - le circuit ISA et 10 ensembles de ses valeurs de "
"paramètres.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Append the samplex item to the `QuantumProgram` with these arguments:\n"
"- The template circuit and the samplex generated by the `build` function\n"
"- Ten sets of parameter values for the original circuit\n"
"- The number of randomizations to perform\n"
msgstr ""
"Ajouter l'élément samplex au `QuantumProgram` avec ces arguments :\n"
"- Le circuit template et le samplex générés par la fonction `build`\n"
"- Dix ensembles de valeurs de paramètres pour le circuit original\n"
"- Le nombre de randomisations à effectuer\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Run the Executor job {#run-the-executor-job}"
msgstr "Exécuter le job Executor {#run-the-executor-job}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Retrieve the result for each task.\n"
msgstr "Récupérer le résultat pour chaque tâche.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Example: Perform PEC {#example-perform-pec}"
msgstr "Exemple : Effectuer une PEC {#example-perform-pec}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This example shows how to use a samplex item to perform probabilistic error "
"cancellation ([PEC](/guides/error-mitigation-and-suppression-"
"techniques#pec)) for error mitigation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cet exemple montre comment utiliser un élément samplex pour effectuer la "
"cancellation d'erreurs probabiliste ([PEC](/guides/error-mitigation-and-"
"suppression-techniques#pec)) pour la mitigation d'erreurs.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider a mirrored-version of a circuit with ten qubits and two unique layers of CX gates. These are the main tasks:\n"
"- Execute the circuit with twirling.\n"
"- Execute the circuit with PEC mitigation, as in the paper [\"Probabilistic error cancellation with sparse Pauli-Lindblad models on noisy quantum processors\"](https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.09866).\n"
msgstr ""
"Considérons une version miroir d'un circuit avec dix qubits et deux couches uniques de gates CX. Ce sont les tâches principales :\n"
"- Exécuter le circuit avec twirling.\n"
"- Exécuter le circuit avec la mitigation PEC, comme dans l'article [«Probabilistic error cancellation with sparse Pauli-Lindblad models on noisy quantum processors»](https://arxiv.org/abs/2201.09866).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The pipeline consists of these steps:\n"
"1. Set up: Generate the target circuit and group its operations into boxes.\n"
"2. Learn: Learn the noise of the instructions that we want to mitigate with PEC.\n"
"3. Execute: Run the circuit on a backend.\n"
"4. Analyze: Post-process and analyze the results.\n"
msgstr ""
"Le pipeline consiste en ces étapes :\n"
"1. Configuration : Générer le circuit cible et regrouper ses opérations dans des boîtes.\n"
"2. Apprentissage : Apprendre le bruit des instructions que nous voulons mitiger avec PEC.\n"
"3. Exécution : Exécuter le circuit sur un backend.\n"
"4. Analyse : Post-traiter et analyser les résultats.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For comparison, we will run this mirrored circuit twice. Once with only "
"Pauli-twirling applied, and once withe PEC mitigation applied.\n"
msgstr ""
"À titre de comparaison, nous allons exécuter ce circuit miroir deux fois. "
"Une fois avec seulement le Pauli-twirling appliqué, et une fois avec la "
"mitigation PEC appliquée.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"The usage for this example is approximately 10 minutes on a Heron r2 processor.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"L'utilisation pour cet exemple est d'environ 10 minutes sur un processeur Heron r2.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set up the circuit {#set-up-the-circuit-1}"
msgstr "Configurer le circuit {#set-up-the-circuit-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a backend and prepare a 10-qubit circuit.\n"
msgstr "Choisir un backend et préparer un circuit à 10 qubits.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/executor-"
"examples/extracted-outputs/f9e93b2c-154a-4d09-872d-f770bcc669c4-0.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/executor-"
"examples/extracted-outputs/f9e93b2c-154a-4d09-872d-f770bcc669c4-0.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Combine the circuit with its inverse to create a mirror circuit.\n"
msgstr "Combiner le circuit avec son inverse pour créer un circuit miroir.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/executor-"
"examples/extracted-outputs/f8ac3f75-88ca-40f9-8382-6a427303bb8e-0.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/guides/executor-"
"examples/extracted-outputs/f8ac3f75-88ca-40f9-8382-6a427303bb8e-0.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Set some parameter values:\n"
msgstr "Définir quelques valeurs de paramètres :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use the pass manager to transpile the circuit to become an ISA circuit.\n"
msgstr ""
"Utiliser le pass manager pour transpiler le circuit en un circuit ISA.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, group gates and measurements into annotated boxes. You can do this "
"manually or use the `generate_boxing_pass_manager` function from Samplomatic"
" for convenience. The first circuit will only have twirling applied and "
"therefore only needs the `Twirl` annotation. The second circuit will be run "
"with full PEC mitigation and needs both `Twirl` and `InjectNoise` "
"annotations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ensuite, regrouper les gates et les mesures dans des boîtes annotées. Tu "
"peux le faire manuellement ou utiliser la fonction "
"`generate_boxing_pass_manager` de Samplomatic pour plus de commodité. Le "
"premier circuit n'aura que le twirling appliqué et n'a donc besoin que de "
"l'annotation `Twirl`. Le deuxième circuit sera exécuté avec une mitigation "
"PEC complète et a besoin des annotations `Twirl` et `InjectNoise`.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Learn the noise {#learn-the-noise}"
msgstr "Apprendre le bruit {#learn-the-noise}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To minimize the number of noise learning experiments, identify the unique instructions in the second circuit (the one with boxes annotated with `InjectNoise`). In defining uniqueness, two box instructions are equal if both of the following are true:\n"
"- Their content is equal, up to single-qubit gates.\n"
"- Their `Twirl` annotation is equal (every other annotation is disregarded).\n"
msgstr ""
"Pour minimiser le nombre d'expériences d'apprentissage du bruit, identifier les instructions uniques dans le deuxième circuit (celui avec les boîtes annotées avec `InjectNoise`). Pour définir l'unicité, deux instructions de boîte sont égales si les deux conditions suivantes sont vraies :\n"
"- Leur contenu est égal, à des gates à un qubit près.\n"
"- Leur annotation `Twirl` est égale (toute autre annotation est ignorée).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This leads to three unique instructions, namely the odd and even gate boxes,"
" and the final measurement box.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cela conduit à trois instructions uniques, à savoir les boîtes de gates "
"pairs et impairs, et la boîte de mesure finale.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Initialize a `NoiseLearnerV3`, choose the learning parameters by setting its"
" options, and run a noise learning job.\n"
msgstr ""
"Initialiser un `NoiseLearnerV3`, choisir les paramètres d'apprentissage en "
"définissant ses options, et exécuter un job d'apprentissage du bruit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Convert `result` to the object required by the samplex by using the "
"`result.to_dict` method.\n"
msgstr ""
"Convertir `result` en objet requis par le samplex en utilisant la méthode "
"`result.to_dict`.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Execute the circuits {#execute-the-circuits-1}"
msgstr "Exécuter les circuits {#execute-the-circuits-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`Executor` runs `QuantumProgram` objects. Each `QuantumProgram` can contain "
"several *items*, which are appended to the program. Each item is a task for "
"the program to perform.\n"
msgstr ""
"`Executor` exécute des objets `QuantumProgram`. Chaque `QuantumProgram` peut"
" contenir plusieurs *éléments*, qui sont ajoutés au programme. Chaque "
"élément est une tâche que le programme doit effectuer.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Initialize an empty program, requesting `1000` shots for each configuration "
"of each item.\n"
msgstr ""
"Initialiser un programme vide, en demandant `1000` shots pour chaque "
"configuration de chaque élément.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, build the template circuit and samplex for `mirror_circuit_twirl` and "
"append them to the program. Also request `900` randomizations from the "
"samplex. This means that the samplex will generate `900` sets of parameters,"
" and each set will be executed `1000` times (the number of shots) in the "
"QPU.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ensuite, construire le circuit template et le samplex pour "
"`mirror_circuit_twirl` et les ajouter au programme. Également demander `900`"
" randomisations au samplex. Cela signifie que le samplex générera `900` "
"ensembles de paramètres, et chaque ensemble sera exécuté `1000` fois (le "
"nombre de shots) sur le QPU.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This is the program's first task (result 0).\n"
msgstr "C'est la première tâche du programme (résultat 0).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Similarly, append the template circuit and samplex built for "
"`mirror_circuit_pec`, requesting `900` randomizations.  This is the "
"program's second task (result 1).\n"
msgstr ""
"De même, ajouter le circuit template et le samplex construits pour "
"`mirror_circuit_pec`, en demandant `900` randomisations. C'est la deuxième "
"tâche du programme (résultat 1).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Import `Executor` and submit a job.\n"
msgstr "Importer `Executor` et soumettre un job.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Analyze results {#analyze-results}"
msgstr "Analyser les résultats {#analyze-results}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, post-process the results to estimate the expectation values of "
"single-qubit Pauli-Z operators acting on each of the ten active qubits "
"(expected value: `1.0`).\n"
msgstr ""
"Enfin, post-traiter les résultats pour estimer les valeurs d'espérance des "
"opérateurs de Pauli-Z à un qubit agissant sur chacun des dix qubits actifs "
"(valeur attendue : `1.0`).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Prochaines étapes {#next-steps}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- Review the [broadcasting](/guides/primitive-input-output#broadcasting) overview.\n"
"- Learn how to use [Executor options](/guides/executor-options).\n"
"- Understand the [directed execution model](/guides/directed-execution-model).\n"
"- Review the [Samplomatic documentation](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/).\n"
"- Learn about how to combine different error mitigation techniques when using directed execution model in the [Probabilistic error cancellation with shaded lightcones](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-slc/tutorials/01_getting_started.html) tutorial.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommandations\">\n"
"- Consulte l'aperçu du [broadcasting](/guides/primitive-input-output#broadcasting).\n"
"- Apprends à utiliser les [options d'Executor](/guides/executor-options).\n"
"- Comprends le [modèle d'exécution dirigée](/guides/directed-execution-model).\n"
"- Consulte la [documentation Samplomatic](https://qiskit.github.io/samplomatic/).\n"
"- Apprends à combiner différentes techniques de mitigation d'erreurs lors de l'utilisation du modèle d'exécution dirigée dans le tutoriel [Probabilistic error cancellation with shaded lightcones](https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-slc/tutorials/01_getting_started.html).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
